From 8d5a93359167d1dfe4b29402434fb85c14b62fbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patch <patch@local>
Date: Tue, 26 May 2026 21:49:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] modwlan: expose libwifi 802.11 frame parsing via
 WLAN.parse_frame()

Adds a new method WLAN.parse_frame(buf) that takes a raw 802.11 MAC
frame (typically obtained from WLAN.wifi_packet().data while in
promiscuous mode) and returns an attrtuple describing the frame.

The base attrtuple has fields:
  type, subtype, flags (to_ds/from_ds/retry/protect/...),
  duration, addr1, addr2, addr3, seq, frag, body, detail

For management subtypes that libwifi has rich parsers for (beacon,
probe req/resp, (re)assoc req/resp, deauth, disassoc), 'detail' is a
subtype-specific attrtuple. For beacons/probe_resp it includes ssid,
bssid, channel, encryption_info bitfield, security/ciphers/akm strings,
and a [(tag_num, bytes)] list of all 802.11 tagged parameters.

Also exposes WLAN.FRAME_MGMT / FRAME_CTRL / FRAME_DATA / FRAME_EXT and
WLAN.SUBTYPE_* constants so callers don't need libwifi enum imports
from Python.

Gated behind MOD_LIBWIFI_ENABLED (default on for WIPY, off elsewhere).

Typical usage:

  from network import WLAN
  w = WLAN(mode=WLAN.STA)
  w.promiscuous(True)
  pkt = w.wifi_packet()
  info = w.parse_frame(pkt.data)
  if info and info.type == WLAN.FRAME_MGMT \
      and info.subtype == WLAN.SUBTYPE_BEACON:
      print(info.detail.ssid, info.detail.bssid, info.detail.security)

Memory: every libwifi struct that owns heap (tags, body, radiotap_info)
is fully copied into MicroPython-owned objects before libwifi_free_* is
called. No dangling pointers possible from Python.
